   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- **Where dates come from:** `store.add` stores `created` as `moment.isoformat()` (`fieldnotes/store.py:24`). That gives a string like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`.\n- **How `list` prints them:** `list` prints `note['created']` unchanged (`fieldnotes/cli.py:19`). It does no locale formatting, `strftime` or `toLocale` conversion.\n- **Other date output:** these are the only two places in the package that touch dates. `add` prints only the note text.\n\nI only read the code and didn't run `list`. I also didn't open `tools/check.py` or `README.md`, so I haven't checked them for date formats.\n\nIf a note in `notes.json` was written by hand or by an older version, `list` would print its `created` value as stored. It never normalizes the value.",
