   "reply": "I added an `export` command that prints one line per note as `DATE: TEXT`. The project checks pass: 2 tests ran and the line-length rule is clean.\n\n- **Command:** `fieldnotes/cli.py` now handles `export`, and the usage message mentions it.\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the note's full stored ISO timestamp, for example `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00: first`. If you want only the date part, it's a one-line change.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_cli.py` adds two notes, runs `cli.main([\"export\"])`, and checks the exit code and both output lines.\n- **Check setup:** `tools/check.py` requires `NOTES_HOME`, so I ran it with that set to a temporary directory.",
